          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %strong Cat
            is a name for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} categories
          %p
            This is also the archetypical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} 2-topos
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            To avoid set-theoretic problems related to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Russell%27s+paradox"} Russell's paradox
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            to
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CAT"} CAT
            for alternatives.
          %p
            To be explicit, define
            %strong Cat
            to be the category with:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small categories
                as
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} objects
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functors
                as
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphisms
            %li
              %p composition of morphisms the evident composition of functors.
          %p
            This is probably the most common meaning of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            in the literature.
          %p
            We more often use
            %strong Cat
            to stand for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-category
            with:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small categories
              as
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} objects
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functors
              as
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphisms
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformations
              as
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphisms
          %p
            Here the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+composition"} vertical composition
            of 2-morphisms is the evident composition of component maps of natural transformations, whereas the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"} horizontal composition
            is given by their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Godement+product"} Godement product
          %p
            Finally, we can use
            %strong Cat
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            with:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small categories
              as
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} objects
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctors
              as
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphisms
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ananatural+transformation"} ananatural transformations
              as
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphisms
          %p
            To be really careful, this version of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anabicategory"} anabicategory
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#CartesianClosedStructure Cartesian closed structure
          %p
            The category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed"} cartesian closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+objects"} exponential objects
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+categories"} functor categories
          %ul
            %li
              p. 98 of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+Work"} Categories Work
            %li
              remark below Definition 4.3.9 in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Category+Theory+in+Context"} Category Theory in Context
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Awodey"}> Steve Awodey
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Category Theory
          %p
            A more indirect proof could proceed by identifying
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            construction as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+ideal"} exponential ideal
          %h3#size_issues Size issues
          %p
            As a
            = succeed "-category," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            could even include (some)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} large categories
            without running into Russell’s paradox. More precisely, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+universe"} Grothendieck universe
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Set
            is the category of all
            = succeed "-small" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Cat
            to be the 2-category of all
            = succeed "-small" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U'
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U'
            is some Grothendieck universe containing
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Set \in \Cat
            without contradiction. (This can be continued to
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher categories
          %p
            By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            as a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} category
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Str
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str Cat
            for the strict
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            in the anabicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            iff it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Str
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            as obtained from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Str
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str Cat
            using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            by “formally inverting” the essentially surjective and fully faithful functors as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
          %h3#limits_and_colimits Limits and colimits
          %p
          #OrdinaryLimitsAndColimits.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %em (ordinary limits and colimits of categories)
              %br/
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+categories"} small categories
              is
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicomplete+category"} bicomplete
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi I
                        %mo →
                        %mi Cat
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{(-)} \,\colon\, I \to Cat
                  is computed componentwise: the sets of objects and of morphisms of the limiting category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ⟵
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim} F
                  are the limits in
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Obj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi I
                        %mo →
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Obj(\mathcal{C}_{(-)}) \,\colon\, I \to Set
                  and of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Mor
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi I
                          %mo →
                          %mi Set
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(\mathcal{C}_{(-)}) \,\colon\, I \to Set
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi I
                        %mo →
                        %mi Cat
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{(-)} \,\colon\, I \to Cat
                  is on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  still the colimit of the underlying diagram of sets of objects, but on morphisms it is more complicated, since in the naive colimit of sets of morphisms some morphisms may become composable that were not composable before.
                %p
                  An exception is the case of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                  of categories, which are just given componentwise by
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "colimit#ColimitsInTermsOfCoequalizers"} this Prop
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizers"} coequalizers
                  of functors exist.
                %p
                  Explicit formulas for coequalizers of categories are given in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "#BednarczykBorzyszkowskiPawlowski99"} Bednarczyk, Borzyszkowski &amp; Pawlowski 1999, §4
                %p
                  Moreover, formulas for
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
                  in
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                  of injective functors are discussed in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "#MacdonalScull09"} MacDonald &amp; Scull 2009
            %p
          %p
            See also discussion at
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/q/272479/58526"} MO:q/272479
